{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "A Day With Vanessa"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Talking about Work"}, {"type": "position", "content": 6}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 16}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Use expressions about relationships and feelings in a range of social and work contexts. "}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Subject and Object Relative Clauses"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When you want to clarify which person or thing you are talking about, you use a relative clause.<br/><br/>You can begin a relative clause with <span class=\"italic\">who</span> for people, <span class=\"italic\">which</span> for things or <span class=\"italic\">that</span> for either people or things.<br/><br/>In spoken English you usually use <span class=\"italic\">that</span>, rather than <span class=\"italic\">which</span> or <span class=\"italic\">who</span>.<br/><br/>You put the relative clause immediately after the noun it talks about."}, {"type": "text", "content": "A subject relative clause describes the subject of the clause."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Example</span>:<br/><span class=\"italic\">The man <span class=\"strong\">who/that</span> called wanted to speak to Tom.</span><br/>Which man? The man who called.<br/>The clause <span class=\"italic\">who called</span> immediately follows <span class=\"italic\">man</span> - the noun it describes."}, {"type": "text", "content": "An object relative clause describes the object of the clause."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Example</span>:<br/><span class=\"italic\">The book <span class=\"strong\">which/that</span> I lent you was my father's.</span><br/>Which book? The book I lent you."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Native speakers of English often omit the pronoun in object clauses. <br/>For example:<br/>The book I lent you was my father's."}, {"type": "example", "content": "The woman who is riding the bike is my boss."}, {"type": "example", "content": "The man that's sitting on the bench is my friend."}, {"type": "example", "content": "There's a great view of the park which I love."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Talking About the Future - If, When, Before and After"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use time clauses to give information about time and sequence."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the words If, When, Before and After in time clauses."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the first conditional with these time clauses."}, {"type": "text", "content": "If/When/Before/After + Subject + Simple Present tense, Subject + will/be going to + Simple Present tense"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Before</span> means at an earlier time."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">After</span> means at a later time."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">Before I go to sleep, I'll set my alarm.<br/>After I set my alarm, I'm going to go to sleep.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">If</span> means on the condition that ..."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">If I go to sleep, I'll set my alarm.</span> (I'm not sure that I'll go to sleep)."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">When</span> means at the time of doing something."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">When I go to bed, I'll set my alarm.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": " I'll do some research about it when I get home."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Before you do that, let's try to guess! "}, {"type": "example", "content": "If they have a miniature horse sculpture in the gift shop, I'm going to buy it! "}, {"type": "example", "content": "After this, are we going to go for lunch? "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to hack"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to deal with something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I can't hack seeing her right now."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le16ob06aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about jobs or work."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "the coast is clear"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "there is no danger of being seen"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Ask him if the coast is clear. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le16ob06aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to give the all clear"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to announce when a dangerous situation is over"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: After he gives me the all clear, then I'll head to my desk."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le16ob06aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "fear"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the state of being afraid"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Sometimes with respect comes a little fear ..."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le16ob06aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "terror"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a person who inspires great fear"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I don't want to be a terror! "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le16ob06aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "dreadful"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "horrible; terrible"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: That's got to be dreadful for the staff. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le16ob06aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn7le16ob06re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Think about what kind of boss you want to have."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Brainstorm some ways to describe a great boss."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make a list of things that make a boss great to work for."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Compare your list with a par